<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patricio Aylwin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–2016</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patricio Aylwin was a Chilean Christian Democrat politician and the first president after the military regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a>. Elected at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concertacion">Concertación</a> coalition, he governed from 1990 to 1994. His government set up the Rettig Commission to investigate killings and disappearances under the dictatorship, while Pinochet remained commander of the army.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patricio-aylwin.jpg" alt="Patricio Aylwin" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Biblioteca del Congreso Nacional de Chile · CC BY 3.0 cl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aylwin_Banda_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
